<div class="reading"><p class="eyebrow">A clear path, a thoughtful handoff</p><h1>Neighbors helping neighbors.</h1><h2 id="connect" tabindex="-1">For people giving</h2><p>Describe one item and provide 1–5 photographs. A moderator reviews the listing and recall information before publication. Respond to one requester at a time. Making an offer is not a reservation: the recipient must accept.</p><h2>For people receiving</h2><p>Browse without an account. Sign in by phone code when requesting. Gift and loan requests require identity and location evidence and request-specific consent before they reach a donor, subject to approved privacy controls.</p><p>A caregiver or community helper can use their own account to assist someone else.</p><div id="handoff" tabindex="-1"><div class="note"><b>Meet safely, together.</b><br>Arrange pickup or return in a public, nonresidential place, in daylight while the venue is open. FreeDME does not inspect equipment, arrange transport or guarantee returns. Decline an item that seems unsafe or unsuitable.</div></div><h2>Know what the service can and cannot do</h2><p>Equipment is free. FreeDME does not inspect, certify, fit, repair, assemble, deliver or guarantee return of equipment. Condition and capacity are donor-reported. Seek qualified advice for fit and use; do not test uncertain equipment by putting yourself at risk.</p><section id="protection" tabindex="-1"><h2>How we plan to protect the community</h2><p>Phone verification, moderator screening of equipment listings, and tools to report concerns help support the community. These checks do not guarantee equipment safety or another participant’s conduct.</p><p>Signup in the current design asks for a display name, mobile number, and approximate location. Before a gift or loan request is sent to a donor, the requester supplies identity and address evidence; the donor sees the verified name and ZIP code. Caregivers provide their own evidence.</p><p>Questions and answers are shown in the participants’ activity pages rather than public listings. This demo simulates verification and SMS; production privacy controls and evidence-retention choices still require approval.</p></section><h2>When plans change</h2><p>Cancel or report a concern in My activity. A cancellation, due date or silence never automatically makes a reserved item available. The donor must confirm possession and availability, and safety holds must be resolved.</p><h2>Time to respond</h2><p>Pending requests receive a reminder at 24 hours and close at 48 hours. Offers last 24 hours. Details of other reminders, listing freshness and loan timing remain open for approval.</p><div class="actions"><button class="primary" data-action="browse" data-id="">Find equipment</button><button class="" data-action="donate" data-id="">Donate equipment</button></div></div>